Read-only trace: the machine build ran golden's generic two-arm DoTestHeadMotor (Frank's DoTestHeadMotorFP, the order of EastSun's
list, was #ifdef SOFT_SIMULTE), and Prod.TestZ1_Safe was raised to golden's minimum iGalil_Z_SafePos = +200 -- above home on HT9050
(home 0, down negative), so the shuttles' Z1-at-safe wait (acarry.cpp W906_Ht9050Z1AtSafe, +-10) could never clear.
- csystem.cpp DoAllProcess Index slot: `#ifdef SOFT_SIMULTE` -> `#if 1` (HT9050 -> DoTestHeadMotorFP in SIM and SHIP; others unchanged).
- cinitial.cpp SetTechDataToProd_Index: HT9050 (9050GPIB or Type_HT9050) TestZ1_Safe = TestZ2_Safe = 0. Same lines.
- tests/test_fp9050_index.cpp: [SIM9050] pins `#if 1`; [F2] census exempts the two FP entry points in csystem.cpp (the old exact-text
  exemption never matched -- the lines were #ifdef'd out of the SHIP scan).
FP9050_Pure, FP9050_Index, Flow9050_Shuttle, HT9050_ShtSafe, E044TorqueWait, HT9050_DryRun, Flow9050_Tray, HT9050_ProdFlow passed (SHIP).
Release linked; Debug compiled (link waits for EastSun's program). Backups D:\HT9045\_review\*.bak_fpmachine_20261007_210536. WORKLOG row 184.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
